   "problem": {
    "en": "R = 10 kΩ and C = 0.1 µF. Find the time constant. Will this circuit differentiate or integrate a 50 Hz square wave, and where is the output taken?"
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "τ = RC = 10⁴ × 10⁻⁷ = 10⁻³ s = 1 ms."
    },
    {
     "en": "For 50 Hz, T = 20 ms, so RC << T."
    },
    {
     "en": "Taking the output across R, it works as a differentiator: sharp spikes at each edge."
    },
    {
     "en": "To integrate a 50 Hz wave, RC should be much more than 20 ms (for example 100 kΩ and 10 µF gives 1 s)."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "τ = 1 ms; a differentiator with output across R"
